cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MultimodalVA: cause-of-death classification from verbal autopsy data"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yue
    family-names: Chu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8671-5362"
    affiliation: "The Ohio State University"
    email: ychu612@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/y-chu/MultimodalVA"
url: "https://github.com/y-chu/MultimodalVA"
abstract: >-
  A Python package for cause-of-death classification from verbal autopsy data.
  It provides a single interface over text-only, tabular-only and multimodal
  workflows, covering transformer fine-tuning, scikit-learn tabular models,
  hyperparameter search, four ensemble methods spanning data-, feature- and
  decision-level fusion, and evaluation utilities
  including CSMF accuracy and probability calibration.
keywords:
  - verbal autopsy
  - cause of death
  - clinical NLP
  - multimodal learning
  - health surveillance
  - global health
license: MIT
